Here's a comprehensive prompt you can give to an AI coding assistant (or use later with me) to refactor your PWA onboarding flow.

---

```text
I want to redesign my PWA onboarding experience to follow modern mobile UX practices similar to Starbucks, Instagram, TikTok, and other high-conversion PWAs.

The goal is to maximize install rate and notification opt-in while avoiding annoying users.

========================================
GENERAL GOALS
========================================

• Make every prompt feel like a native mobile bottom sheet.
• Use smooth animations.
• Never overwhelm users with multiple permission requests.
• Focus on explaining BENEFITS instead of FEATURES.
• Keep the experience modern, minimal, and premium.
• Mobile-first design.

========================================
PWA INSTALL PROMPT
========================================

Do NOT ask users to install immediately.

Instead, intelligently decide based on engagement.

Priority triggers:

1. User successfully places an order (highest priority)
2. User logs into their account
3. User creates a wishlist
4. User has visited around 8–10 pages
5. User has spent meaningful time on the website



========================================
DISMISS LOGIC
========================================

Do NOT permanently dismiss the prompt.

Instead:

Save the dismissal timestamp.

Show it again after 3 days.

If installed:

Save installed status permanently.

Listen for:

window.addEventListener('appinstalled', ...)

instead of relying only on beforeinstallprompt.

========================================
INSTALL COPY
========================================

Use modern wording.

Title:

Get the Full LULU Experience

Body:

Install LULU for faster shopping, instant order updates, and one-tap access directly from your home screen.

Buttons:

Install App
Maybe Later

Avoid technical terms like:

PWA
Progressive Web App

========================================
IOS INSTALL PROMPT
========================================

Explain WHY.

Example:

Install LULU in seconds.

Tap Share and choose Add to Home Screen to enjoy faster shopping and quick access anytime.

Button:

Got It

========================================
NOTIFICATION FLOW
========================================

Never request notification permission immediately after installation.

Instead:

User installs app

↓

User uses app

↓

Places an order

OR

Returns later

↓

Ask for notifications.

This should feel earned.

========================================
NOTIFICATION COPY
========================================

Title:

Never Miss an Update

Body:

Receive order confirmations, shipping updates, delivery alerts, and exclusive offers right on your device.

Buttons:

Allow Notifications
Not Now

Do NOT use:

Enable Notifications

========================================
NOTIFICATION COOLDOWN
========================================

If user dismisses notification prompt:

Store timestamp.

Ask again after 3 days.

Do not permanently suppress it.

========================================
ANIMATIONS
========================================

Use a premium bottom-sheet animation.

Initial state:

opacity: 0;
transform: translateY(30px) scale(.96);

Visible:

opacity: 1;
transform: translateY(0) scale(1);

Animation:

300ms
ease

========================================
TIMING
========================================

Avoid fixed delays when possible.

Prefer:

requestIdleCallback()

with a setTimeout fallback.

Only display prompts when the UI is idle.

========================================
EVENT LISTENERS
========================================

Prevent duplicate listeners.

Do NOT attach addEventListener() every time the prompt opens.

Use:

button.onclick = ...

or initialize listeners once.

========================================
INSTALL DETECTION
========================================

Detect:

display-mode: standalone

navigator.standalone

appinstalled event

Keep localStorage synchronized with the install status.

========================================
OVERALL FLOW
========================================

First visit

↓

No prompts

↓

User browses

↓

Build engagement score

↓

Show install prompt

↓

Dismiss

↓

Wait 3 days

↓

Ask again

↓

User installs

↓

Uses app

↓

Places order

↓

Show notification prompt

↓

Dismiss

↓

Wait 14 days

↓

Ask again

========================================
CODE REQUIREMENTS
========================================

• Keep code clean and modular.
• Separate engagement logic from UI logic.
• Avoid duplicated code.
• Prevent duplicate event listeners.
• Make it easy to add future onboarding steps.
• Keep Laravel compatibility.
• Preserve existing functionality where possible while improving architecture and UX.
```

This prompt gives enough context and specific requirements to produce a much more polished onboarding system that balances conversion with a good user experience.
